<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Privacy — The Crawl Price Index</title>
<meta name="description" content="What personal data the Crawl Price Index collects, why, on what legal basis, how long it is kept, and how to exercise your rights.">
<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns=%27http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%27 viewBox=%270 0 32 32%27%3E%3Crect width=%2732%27 height=%2732%27 fill=%27%23FBFAF8%27/%3E%3Crect x=%276%27 y=%2714%27 width=%2720%27 height=%274%27 fill=%27%231C5D4A%27/%3E%3C/svg%3E">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,300;0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;1,6..72,300&family=Archivo:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  *{box-sizing:border-box}
  body{margin:0;background:var(--ink);color:var(--fg);font-family:"Newsreader",Georgia,serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.6}
  a{color:var(--signal)}
  h2{font-size:22px;font-weight:500;color:var(--bright);margin:38px 0 10px}
  table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:14px 0;font-size:15px}
  th,td{text-align:left;padding:10px 10px 10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top}
  th{font-family:"Spline Sans Mono",monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--dim);font-weight:500}
  code{font-family:"Spline Sans Mono",monospace;font-size:13.5px;color:var(--bright);background:#161a1c;padding:1px 5px}
  .box{background:var(--panel);border-left:3px solid var(--signal);padding:15px 17px;margin:20px 0}
  ul{padding-left:22px} li{margin-bottom:7px}
  footer{margin-top:52px;padding:22px 0 60px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-family:"Spline Sans Mono",monospace;font-size:12px;color:var(--dim)}
</style>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/theme.css">
</head>
<body class="prose">
<div class="masthead"><div class="wrap">
  <a class="mark" href="/">The Crawl Price Index<b>.</b></a>
  <nav class="navmid">
    <a class="lnk" href="/why">Why it matters</a>
    <a class="lnk" href="/check">Check a domain</a>
    <a class="lnk" href="/explore">Explore data</a>
    <a class="lnk" href="/methodology">Method</a>
    <a class="lnk" href="/about">About</a>
  </nav>
  <div class="navend">
    <a class="btn ghostbox" href="https://app.crawlpriceindex.com">Sign in</a>
    <a class="btn" href="https://app.crawlpriceindex.com/dashboard.html#account">Full dataset &mdash; &euro;49/mo</a>
  </div>
</div></div>
<div class="page-open"><div class="wrap">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p style="margin:0;max-width:620px">Short version: we collect an email address if you ask us to send you something, and nothing else. No advertising, no tracking pixels, no third-party analytics, no cookies for marketing.</p>
  <div class="meta">Last updated 11 August 2026 · <a href="mailto:hello@crawlpriceindex.com">hello@crawlpriceindex.com</a></div>
</div></div>

<div class="wrap"><div class="panels">
<section class="panel wide">
  <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">Who is responsible</span></div>
  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
<p>The Crawl Price Index is operated by Alexander Balieu, sole trader, based in Luxembourg, acting as data controller. Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@crawlpriceindex.com">hello@crawlpriceindex.com</a>. Postal address available on request.</p>

</section>
<section class="panel wide">
  <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">What we collect, why, and on what basis</span></div>
  <h2>What we collect, why, and on what basis</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Data</th><th>Why</th><th>Legal basis (GDPR Art. 6)</th><th>Kept</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Email address (newsletter / data sample)</td><td>To send The Weekly Crawl and your sample link</td><td>Consent — 6(1)(a), given by confirming via the double opt-in email</td><td>Until you unsubscribe, then deleted</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Email address + domain (change alerts)</td><td>To tell you when AI-crawler access to that domain changes</td><td>Consent — 6(1)(a), confirmed by email</td><td>Until you stop the alert, then deleted</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Email address, name, billing details (subscribers)</td><td>To provide the subscription, issue your API key, and meet invoicing and tax obligations</td><td>Contract — 6(1)(b); legal obligation — 6(1)(c) for accounting records</td><td>Duration of the subscription, then as long as tax law requires</td></tr>
  <tr><td>API key usage counts</td><td>To enforce the monthly rate limit and detect abuse</td><td>Contract — 6(1)(b); legitimate interests — 6(1)(f)</td><td>Rolling monthly counter</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Blockchain payment reference (machine tier)</td><td>To verify a payment and prevent the same one being redeemed twice</td><td>Contract — 6(1)(b)</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="box">
<b>We do not:</b> run advertising or marketing cookies · use third-party analytics · sell, rent or share your data with anyone for their own purposes · build profiles · make automated decisions with legal effects about you · collect special-category data.
</div>

</section>
<section class="panel">
  <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">Who processes data on our behalf</span></div>
  <h2>Who processes data on our behalf</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>Cloudflare</b> — hosting, DNS, and storage of subscriber records and keys.</li>
  <li><b>Stripe</b> — subscription payments and invoicing. Stripe is the payment processor and an independent controller for its own compliance purposes; we never see or store full card details.</li>
  <li><b>Resend</b> — sending transactional and newsletter email.</li>
</ul>
<p>Each is bound by a data-processing agreement. Some may process data outside the EEA under the European Commission's standard contractual clauses.</p>

</section>
<section class="panel">
  <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">Server logs</span></div>
  <h2>Server logs</h2>
<p>Our hosting provider processes standard request data (IP address, user agent, timestamp) transiently to deliver the site and protect it from abuse, on the basis of legitimate interests — GDPR Art. 6(1)(f). We do not build analytics from it, and we do not use it to identify visitors.</p>

</section>
<section class="panel">
  <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">Your rights</span></div>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>Under the GDPR you may request access to your data, correction, erasure, restriction, portability, or object to processing based on legitimate interests. Where processing rests on consent, you may withdraw it at any time — every email we send carries a one-click unsubscribe link, which deletes the record rather than merely flagging it.</p>
<p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@crawlpriceindex.com">hello@crawlpriceindex.com</a> and we will respond within 30 days. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Luxembourg supervisory authority, the <a href="https://cnpd.public.lu" rel="noopener">Commission nationale pour la protection des données (CNPD)</a>, or with the authority in your country of residence.</p>

</section>
<section class="panel">
  <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">Data about websites, not people</span></div>
  <h2>Data about websites, not people</h2>
<p>The index itself measures how <em>websites</em> respond to automated crawlers: robots.txt directives, HTTP status codes and payment headers. That is information about domains and their configuration, not about individuals, and we store no page content. Our full method is published in the <a href="/methodology.html">methodology</a> &middot; <a href="/about">about</a>. If you operate a site and want it excluded from the index, email us from a domain-verifiable address and we will remove it.</p>

</section>
<section class="panel">
  <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">Security</span></div>
  <h2>Security</h2>
<p>Data is held in Cloudflare infrastructure. Secrets are stored encrypted and are never in source control. Our crawler signs its own requests cryptographically so sites can verify our traffic. To report a vulnerability, see <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a>.</p>

</section>
<section class="panel">
  <div class="ix"><span class="lead-in">Changes</span></div>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
<p>Material changes to this policy will be noted in the <a href="/changelog.html">changelog</a> with a date. The "last updated" date above always reflects the current version.</p>

</section>
</div></div>
<footer class="sitefoot"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="footlede">
    <h2>The market is being built now. The record starts <em>now</em> too.</h2>
    <p>A week that isn&rsquo;t measured is gone &mdash; no one can reconstruct it later, including us. Every edition is archived the day it is taken.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="footgrid">
    <div class="footcard">
      <div class="fk">Free</div>
      <h3>The free edition</h3>
      <p>Headline figures, the aggregate dashboard and every denominator behind them. Free to cite with attribution.</p>
      <a class="btn ghostbox" href="https://app.crawlpriceindex.com">Open the free edition</a>
    </div>

    <div class="footcard">
      <div class="fk">Free &middot; weekly</div>
      <h3>The Weekly Crawl</h3>
      <p>One email a week: what changed, which way it moved, and the week&rsquo;s figures with their denominators. No forecasts.</p>
      <form class="footform" onsubmit="return cpiSubFoot(event,'privacy')">
        <input id="fsub-privacy" type="email" required autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@company.com">
        <button class="btn" type="submit">Get it weekly</button>
      </form>
      <p class="fmsg" id="fmsg-privacy"></p>
    </div>

    <div class="footcard">
      <div class="fk">&euro;49/mo</div>
      <h3>The full dataset</h3>
      <p>Every domain &times; every tracked crawler, weekly history, the change feed and CSV export. One-off snapshot &euro;29.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="https://app.crawlpriceindex.com/dashboard.html#account">Full dataset &mdash; &euro;49/mo</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="footlinks">
    <div><b>Index</b><a href="/">This edition</a><a href="/explore">Explore data</a><a href="/check">Check a domain</a><a href="/world">Suffix groups</a><a href="/estimate">Estimate the range</a></div>
    <div><b>Method</b><a href="/methodology">Methodology</a><a href="/status">Status &amp; coverage</a><a href="/changelog">Changelog</a><a href="/sample">Free sample</a></div>
    <div><b>Project</b><a href="/about">About</a><a href="/why">Why it matters</a><a href="mailto:hello@crawlpriceindex.com">Contact</a></div>
    <div><b>Legal</b><a href="/terms">Terms &amp; data licence</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/security">Security</a></div>
  </div>

  <div class="footbase">
    <span>THE CRAWL PRICE INDEX &middot; independent observatory of the machine-readable web</span>
    <span>Funded by subscriptions only &mdash; no money from any company in this dataset.</span>
  </div>
</div></footer>
<script>
function cpiSubFoot(e,id){
  e.preventDefault();
  var m=document.getElementById('fmsg-'+id), i=document.getElementById('fsub-'+id);
  var em=(i&&i.value||'').trim(); if(!em) return false;
  m.style.color='var(--dim)'; m.textContent='Signing you up…';
  fetch('https://api.crawlpriceindex.com/v1/subscribe',{method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({email:em})})
    .then(function(r){return r.json();})
    .then(function(j){m.style.color='var(--signal)';m.textContent=(j&&j.message)||'You are in — check your inbox for the free sample.';i.value='';})
    .catch(function(){m.style.color='#A33A2A';m.textContent='Something went wrong — try again in a moment.';});
  return false;
}
</script></div>
</body>
</html>
